> **Resurgence of Black Lung Disease**
> The return of black lung disease in coal country, particularly affecting younger miners, signals serious health and occupational challenges [51950]. Once nearly eradicated, its comeback highlights the urgent need for regulations and preventive measures. With federal budget constraints, the path towards effective solutions appears fraught, raising questions about the political and economic priorities concerning worker health and safety in industries critical to energy and environment sectors.
